{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumdominatingset()"]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE20minimumDominatingSetSay6VertexQzGyF","symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"minimumDominatingSet()","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExactCovering.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1764"},"modules":[{"name":"Covering","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumDominatingSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum dominating set (exact): every vertex is in it or adjacent to one in it, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smaller set is; in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges do"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not matter; isolated vertices are in it. Deterministic, but which minimum set it is depends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the search; for one fixed by a rule, see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumDominatingSet()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumDominatingSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each connected component is solved alone; a vertex adjacent to all the others of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component answers alone. Otherwise branch and reduce: after every choice, an undominated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex with one possible dominator gets it, and a vertex whose undominated closed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neighbourhood lies in another’s is ruled out (a leaf rule that settles paths and many trees","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"outright). The search branches on the most-coverage dominator of an undominated vertex with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the fewest left and prunes on the budget, on the largest coverages, and on a greedy 2-packing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(vertices with no dominator in common, each needing its own; on trees the largest 2-packing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is γ, Meir and Moon 1975). γ comes from a greedy descent and decisions one smaller, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last set found is the answer. Sparse components keep O(n + m) words of state; dense ones","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(mean degree d with d² above c ⌈c \/ 64⌉) use bitset closed neighbourhoods, under 2m words.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Exponential in the component size in the worst case; the search does not check for task","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cancellation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumDominatingSet()"},"references":{"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumDominatingSet()":{"abstract":[{"text":"A minimum dominating set (exact): every vertex is in it or adjacent to one in it, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smaller set is; in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges do","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"not matter; isolated vertices are in it. Deterministic, but which minimum set it is depends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the search; for one fixed by a rule, see "},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumDominatingSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","title":"minimumDominatingSet()","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumdominatingset()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumDominatingSet()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumDominatingSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"Covering","url":"\/documentation\/covering","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":